      "body": "### Tested versions\r\n\r\n4.2 stable.\r\n\r\n### System information\r\n\r\nGodot v4.2.stable - Ubuntu 20.04.6 LTS (Focal Fossa) - X11 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 (nvidia; 470.199.02) - AMD FX(tm)-8350 Eight-Core Processor (8 Threads)\r\n\r\n### Issue description\r\n\r\nWhen saving a 3D scene file, I have an object (a door) that always loads at (0,0,0), even though I specify (-2.171, 8.796, -19.122) as its location in the editor:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/assets/55257920/29067074-53ea-4682-9456-c79bfd436ed9)\r\n\r\nThat puts the door where it should be (the orange highlight):\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/assets/55257920/ace93652-1d29-46ac-8abe-98993e32bc22)\r\n\r\nWhen I run the game, the door always appears at (0,0,0). I looked in the *.tscn file, and found that this object doesn't have a Transform3D:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/assets/55257920/e444935f-cc9a-4ee1-823d-3e9f30cf046a)\r\n\r\nI exited the editor, copied a transform from another object, entered the correct coordinates, and reloaded Godot and the project. At that point, the object appeared at its proper location. However, when I run the program, and the editor autosaves, the Transform3D entry in the scene file is once again gone.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\r\n\r\nN/A",
